data: {"type": "TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT", "timestamp": 1793270103794, "messageId": "c1a1e0d7c4", "delta": "Geothermal energy is the heat stored in the ground. A few kilometres down, rock and the water in it are much warmer than at the surface. A doublet taps it with "}

data: {"type": "TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT", "timestamp": 1793270103834, "messageId": "c1a1e0d7c4", "delta": "two wells: one pumps hot water up, a heat exchanger passes its heat to a district network, and the other well returns the cooled water to the same layer. The documentation "}

data: {"type": "TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT", "timestamp": 1793270103874, "messageId": "c1a1e0d7c4", "delta": "counts the wells and everything on the surface as one plant (glossary.rst). The heat is steady through the year, so it suits heating, and with an absorption chiller it can drive "}

data: {"type": "TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT", "timestamp": 1793270103914, "messageId": "c1a1e0d7c4", "delta": "cooling too."}

data: {"type": "TEXT_MESSAGE_END", "timestamp": 1793270103915, "messageId": "c1a1e0d7c4"}

